  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 230 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nFriday-Sunday:\nHigh pressure will quickly settle into the region overnight\nThursday into Friday morning, supporting much cooler\ntemperatures. This will be accompanied by brisk north winds on\nFriday, upwards of 25 to 35 mph. While clouds will gradually\nclear through the day on Friday, highs only reach into the\nmiddle to upper 50s, near 60. The brisk north winds will make it\nfeel more like 40s. As winds lie down and skies clear Friday, a\nrather chilly night is in the forecast.\n\nLows Friday night fall into into the upper 30s to around 40 for\nmost locations, outside of the valleys and protected areas.\nThese areas may see lows closer towards freezing into Saturday\nmorning, in addition to some patchy areas of frost. At this\ntime, confidence remains to low to introduce any frost\nheadlines, but will be monitored in future forecast updates.\n\nHighs rebound into the 60s for Saturday and Sunday, with drier\nweather prevailing. An additional chance for some frost into\nSunday morning, especially across the Eastern Ozarks. \n\nMonday-Tuesday:\nHigh pressure and a ridge gradually build back over the region\nearly next week. This will support a warming trend, with highs\nreturning into the upper 70s to lower 80s. Confidence continues\nto increase on this warm up, as gleaned by the small\ninterquartile spreads and CPC 6 to 10 and 8 to 14 Day above\nnormal temperatures.",
